{
 "where": "inn",
 "clock": "6:00 am",
 "evidence_now": [
  "Tuesday, February 2, 2016. The local radio plays three bright notes and announces a groundhog forecast in the town square. A delivery van backfires twice.",
  "A hotel lobby, a windowsill, a payphone and your coat by the door.",
  "You wake in your bed at the hotel and come down to the lobby.",
  "The windowsill is unmarked.",
  "Today the station has one seven o'clock bulletin. The producer can run the portable switcher from anywhere. The reporter has a phone return; the cameraman has a return for footage he has captured. The station plays its ident if nobody takes the switcher.",
  "The crew's press credentials are clipped to the call sheet: Phil Connors, weather; Rita Hanson, producer; Larry, camera. Location: Punxsutawney, Pennsylvania."
 ],
 "people_in_earshot": [
  "Rita"
 ],
 "remembered_experiences": [
  {
   "morning_observation": "Tuesday, February 2, 2016. The local radio plays three bright notes and announces a groundhog forecast in the town square. A delivery van backfires twice.",
   "episodes_in_order": [
    "6:00 am in inn: Phil reaches the square. Rita says: Phil, good morning—I'm locking the seven o'clock rundown right now. You're on after the ident, live weather, groundhog numbers and all. Got your chart ready? Rita spends the period at the inn. You see Larry at the square. Rita invites Phil on the crew radio to contribute to the evening slot.",
    "9:30 am in square: Phil spends the period at the square. Larry says: Morning, Phil. I'm saving my one take for the band this afternoon — you'll want the switcher queued for the seven, and I'll have festival footage plus that cornet portrait for Rita. Larry spends the period at the square. Phil radios Rita and accepted the evening assignment.",
    "1:00 pm in square: Phil uses the paid ticket and rides the coach all the way to Pittsburgh. Larry says: There you are. One frame, full set—this is the take, Phil. Hold the return open for me after this. Larry uses the camera's last charged take to film the cornet player.",
    "7:00 pm in Pittsburgh: Phil phones the station's live return from Pittsburgh. The seven o'clock broadcast carries Phil's live report from Pittsburgh."
   ],
   "end_of_that_evening": "You fell asleep in Pittsburgh."
  },
  {
   "morning_observation": "Tuesday, February 2, 2016. The local radio plays three bright notes and announces a groundhog forecast in the town square. A delivery van backfires twice.",
   "episodes_in_order": [
    "6:00 am in inn: Phil spends the period at the inn. Rita says: Phil, good morning—I'm locking the seven o'clock rundown right now. You're on after the ident, live weather, groundhog numbers and all. Got your chart ready? Rita spends the period at the inn. Rita invites Phil on the crew radio to contribute to the evening slot.",
    "9:30 am in inn: Phil spends the period at the inn. Rita says: Phil, you're live at the top of the seven o'clock, weather first, then we cut to the town band on the square. Hold position by the bag until I cue you from the switcher. I'm running the ident over you till I'm set up. You're good? Locking it now. Rita spends the period at the inn. Phil radios Rita and accepted the evening assignment.",
    "1:00 pm in inn: Phil uses the paid ticket and rides the coach all the way to Pittsburgh. Rita says: Phil, here's the order: you open at seven with the weather, we cut to the town band live from the square, then Larry's footage, then the close. You locked on that sequence? And I'm putting out a call to Larry now to confirm his tape is ready. Rita spends the period at the inn.",
    "7:00 pm in Pittsburgh: Phil phones the station's live return from Pittsburgh. The seven o'clock broadcast carries Phil's live report from Pittsburgh."
   ],
   "end_of_that_evening": "You fell asleep in Pittsburgh."
  },
  {
   "morning_observation": "Tuesday, February 2, 2016. The local radio plays three bright notes and announces a groundhog forecast in the town square. A delivery van backfires twice.",
   "episodes_in_order": [
    "6:00 am in inn: Phil spends the period at the inn. Rita says: Phil, good morning—I'm locking the seven o'clock rundown right now. You're on after the ident, live weather, groundhog numbers and all. Got your chart ready? Rita spends the period at the inn. Rita invites Phil on the crew radio to contribute to the evening slot.",
    "9:30 am in inn: Phil spends the period at the inn. Rita says: Phil, good. Sit for a sec. I'm locking the seven o'clock rundown now. You're first off, weather, ninety seconds, live from your phone return, right? And after you I want the town band in, maybe sixty seconds of that square performance. You good on that ninety? Rita spends the period at the inn. Phil radios Rita and accepted the evening assignment.",
    "1:00 pm in inn: Phil uses the paid ticket and rides the coach all the way to Pittsburgh. Rita says: Phil, you're set for seven, weather first, then I cut to the band. You told me you needed ten minutes on the phone to lock your chart — did you make that call? And how long are you thinking for the package, two or three? I want to give the band a clean two. Larry, if you've got that rehearsal tape from the square, send it over tonight and I'll build it into the second slot. Rita spends the period at the inn.",
    "7:00 pm in Pittsburgh: Phil phones the station's live return from Pittsburgh. The seven o'clock broadcast carries Phil's live report from Pittsburgh."
   ],
   "end_of_that_evening": "You fell asleep in Pittsburgh."
  },
